    "narrative": "Today\u2019s roster for the Zurich Zebras is anchored by **Yordan Alvarez**, who represents our highest ceiling play with a massive 87.42 efficiency score. He faces a favorable matchup against Rodriguez, whose 5.28 xERA provides the perfect environment for **Yordan Alvarez** to exploit his elite 0.474 xwOBA. Our primary objective remains the aggressive pursuit of Stolen Bases; consequently, **Caleb Durbin** (72.77) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.53) are mandatory starts. **Caleb Durbin** benefits from Lopez\u2019s slow delivery, and while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** faces a difficult pitcher in May, his dynamic platoon advantage and top-of-the-order positioning outweigh the risk of the pitcher\u2019s ability to hold runners. **Dillon Dingler** (63.75) rounds out our high-value targets, capitalizing on a weak opposing arm and his own strong xwOBA to provide significant utility despite the challenging park factors.\n\nThe most difficult decision on our bench was **Chase Meidroth**, who fell just short of our 40.0 efficiency floor at 34.97. While **Chase Meidroth** has shown flashes of productivity, the combination of a high-caliber opposing arm in Schlittler (2.89 xERA) and a suboptimal eighth-spot placement rendered him too risky to start given our current game cap preservation strategy. We are also keeping a close watch on **Carson Benge** (32.80), who remains sidelined not only by a tough matchup against Sale but also by a 45% rain risk that effectively removed him from consideration. We continue to monitor the status of **Kyle Schwarber** and **Colt Keith**, both of whom are currently excluded from their respective team lineups, necessitating that we stay disciplined to our floor requirements to ensure every plate appearance contributes toward our category goals.",
